This directory must exist before the API starts.

app.UseStaticFiles() resolves its WebRootFileProvider once, at startup. With no wwwroot on
disk at that moment it captures a NullFileProvider and every static URL 404s for the life of
the process -- including the /uploads/branding/... URLs the branding upload hands back, which
would make an operator's freshly uploaded logo unreachable until the next restart.

Creating the directory at upload time is too late for exactly that reason, so it is committed.
